```c
dma_spec->np = of_parse_phandle(ofdma->of_node, "dma-masters", 0);
if (!dma_spec->np) {
    dev_err(&pdev->dev, "Can't get DMA master\n");
    return ERR_PTR(-EINVAL);
}
```
Reason:
The function `of_parse_phandle()` increments the reference count of the node pointer it returns. If the function encounters an error (e.g., if `dma_spec->np` is NULL), it returns early without calling `of_node_put()`, which leads to a memory leak because the reference count is not decremented.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
of_node_put(dma_spec->np);
```
Reason:
The added call to `of_node_put(dma_spec->np);` ensures that the reference count of the node pointer is decremented when it is no longer needed, preventing the memory leak that occurs when the function returns early due to an error.

